                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heine-Borel+theorem"} Heine-Borel theorem
                  %p …
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An adaptation of the
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Kendall tau rank correlation
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Kendall+tau+rank+correlation"} ?
            %em Kendall tau distance
            between two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutations"} permutations
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimum"} minimum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} number
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transpositions"} transpositions
            (swaps) of
            %em adjacent
            elements needed to turn one into the other. This quantity can also be defined as the total number of
            %span.newWikiWord
              discordant pairs
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/discordant+pairs"} ?
            between the two
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutations"} permutations
          %p
            (This is in contrast to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley+distance"} Cayley distance
            which counts the minimum number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transpositions"} transpositions
            of any pairs of elements, not necessarily adjacent.)
          %p
            This quantity is also referred to as the
            = succeed "," do
              %em bubble sort distance
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sym
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym(n)
            with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structure"} structure
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+group"} finitely generated group
            exhibited by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators"} generators
            given by the
            %em adjacent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transposition+permutations"} transposition permutations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gen
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi i
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Sym
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Gen
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\big\{
                  \\sigma_{i,i+1}
                  \\,\vert\,
                  1 \leq i \lt n
                  \\big\}
                  \\;\subset\;
                  Sym(n)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then the
            %em Kendall tau distance
            (
            %a{:href => "#Kendall1938"}> Kendall 1938
            , see also
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Diaconis88"} Diaconis 88, p. 112
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distance"} distance
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sym
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym(n)
            which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+distance"} graph distance
            of the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley+graph"} Cayley graph
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Sym
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Sym
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_K(-,-)
                  \\;\colon\;
                  Sym(n) \times Sym(n)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{N}
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{R}
          %p
            which sends any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutations"} permutations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Sym
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_1, \sigma_2 \in Sym(n)
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimum"} minimum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number"} number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(\sigma_1, \sigma_2) \in \mathbb{N}
            of adjacent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transpositions"} transpositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi d
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{i_1, i_1 + 1}, \sigma_{i_2, i_2 + 1}, \cdots, \sigma_{i_d, i_d+1}
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi d
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma_2
                  \\;=\;
                  \\sigma_{i_d, i_d+1}
                  \\circ
                  \\cdots
                  \\circ
                  \\sigma_{i_2, i_2 + 1}
                  \\circ
                  \\sigma_{i_1, i_1 + 1}
                  \\circ
                  \\sigma_1
                  \\,.
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \in \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential"} exponential
            of this distance weighted by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \beta
            is known as the
            = succeed ":" do
              %em Mallows kernel
          #eq:MallowsKernel.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi β
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\sigma_1,\sigma_2)
                  \\;\mapsto\;
                  \\exp
                  \\big(
                  \- \beta d_K(\sigma_1, \sigma_2)
                  \\big)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              The Mallows kernel
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:MallowsKernel"} (1)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+definite+bilinear+form"} positive definite
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \geq 0
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#JiaoVert18"}> Jiao-Vert 18, Theorem 1
            )
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley+distance"} Cayley distance
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mallows+kernel"}> Mallows kernel
                ,
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley+distance+kernel"} Cayley distance kernel
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+kernel"} Markov kernel
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+method"} kernel method
          %h2#references References
          %p The distance function is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Kendall1938
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurice+Kendall"}> Maurice Kendall
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A new measure of rank correlation
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/biomet/30.1-2.81"} doi:10.1093/biomet/30.1-2.81
          %p The corresponding exponential kernel is named after
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C.+L.+Mallows"}> C. L. Mallows
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Non-Null Ranking Models. I
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2333244"} jstor:2333244
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li#Diaconis88
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Persi+Diaconis"}> Persi Diaconis
              , Chapter 6B of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Group Representations in Probability and Statistics
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/i397389"} jstor:i397389
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/ebooks/institute-of-mathematical-statistics-lecture-notes-monograph-series/Group-representations-in-probability-and-statistics/toc/10.1214/lnms/1215467407"} ISBN: 0940600145
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://jdc.math.uwo.ca/M9140a-2012-summer/Diaconis.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kendall_tau_distance"} Kendall tau distance
            %li
              %p
                Cicirello_2020,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kendall tau sequence distance: Extending Kendall tau from ranks to sequences
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.4108/eai.13-7-2018.163925"} DOI=10.4108/eai.13-7-2018.163925
          %p
            Review and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            that the exponentiated negative Kendall tau distance (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mallows+kernel"} Mallows kernel
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+definite+bilinear+form"} positive definite bilinear form
          %ul
            %li#JiaoVert18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yunlong+Jiao"}> Yunlong Jiao
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Philippe+Vert"} Jean-Philippe Vert
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Kendall and Mallows Kernels for Permutations
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1109/TPAMI.2017.2719680"} doi:10.1109/TPAMI.2017.2719680
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/hal-01279273/document"} hal:01279273
          %p Discussion of weighted variants:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yunlong+Jiao"}> Yunlong Jiao
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Philippe+Vert"} Jean-Philippe Vert
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Weighted Kendall and High-order Kernels for Permutations
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.08526"} arXiv:1802.08526
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://proceedings.mlr.press/v80/jiao18a.html"} mlr:v80/jiao18a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://hal.inria.fr/hal-01717385"} hal:hal-01717385
